==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*skakaną}}. Cognate with Old Saxon [[skakan]], Old Norse [[skaka]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈʃɑkɑn/|lang=ang}}

===Verb===
{{ang-verb|type=strong|class=VI}}

# {{context|intransitive|lang=ang}} to [[pass]] or [[depart]]
# {{context|intransitive|lang=ang}} to [[quiver]] or [[vibrate]]
# {{context|transitive|lang=ang}} to [[flourish]] or [[wave]] (an object)
# {{context|transitive|lang=ang}} to cause something to [[quiver]], [[flutter]], or [[shake]]

